 * Constructs an Object of the requested class.
 * The passed class must be a built-in godot class, or an already-registered extension class. In both cases, object_set_instance() should be called to fully initialize the object.
 * 
 * "NOTIFICATION_POSTINITIALIZE" must be sent after construction.
 * @since 4.4
 * @deprecated since 4.7 — use classdb_construct_object3
 */
classdb_construct_object2: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbConstructObject2

/**
 * Constructs an Object of the requested class.
 * The passed class must be a built-in godot class, or an already-registered extension class. In both cases, object_set_instance() should be called to fully initialize the object.
 * If the type is a subtype of RefCounted, it already has a refcount of 1. The caller must take ownership the refcount and is responsible for decrementing it again when the object is no longer needed.
 * 
 * "NOTIFICATION_POSTINITIALIZE" must be sent after construction.
 * @since 4.7
 */
classdb_construct_object3: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbConstructObject3

/**
 * Gets a pointer to the MethodBind in ClassDB for the given class, method and hash.
 * @since 4.1
 */
classdb_get_method_bind: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbGetMethodBind

/**
 * Gets a pointer uniquely identifying the given built-in class in the ClassDB.
 * @since 4.1
 * @deprecated since 4.7
 */
classdb_get_class_tag: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbGetClassTag

/**
 * Registers an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * Provided struct can be safely freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.1
 * @deprecated since 4.2 — use classdb_register_extension_class6
 */
classdb_register_extension_class: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClass

/**
 * Registers an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * Provided struct can be safely freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.2
 * @deprecated since 4.3 — use classdb_register_extension_class6
 */
classdb_register_extension_class2: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClass2

/**
 * Registers an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * Provided struct can be safely freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.3
 * @deprecated since 4.4 — use classdb_register_extension_class6
 */
classdb_register_extension_class3: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClass3

/**
 * Registers an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * Provided struct can be safely freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.4
 * @deprecated since 4.5 — use classdb_register_extension_class6
 */
classdb_register_extension_class4: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClass4

/**
 * Registers an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * Provided struct can be safely freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.5
 * @deprecated since 4.7 — use classdb_register_extension_class6
 */
classdb_register_extension_class5: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClass5

/**
 * Registers an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * Provided struct can be safely freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.7
 */
classdb_register_extension_class6: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClass6

/**
 * Registers a method on an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * Provided struct can be safely freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.1
 */
classdb_register_extension_class_method: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClassMethod

/**
 * Registers a virtual method on an extension class in ClassDB, that can be implemented by scripts or other extensions.
 * Provided struct can be safely freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.3
 */
classdb_register_extension_class_virtual_method: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClassVirtualMethod

/**
 * Registers an integer constant on an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * Note about registering bitfield values (if p_is_bitfield is true): even though p_constant_value is signed, language bindings are
 * advised to treat bitfields as uint64_t, since this is generally clearer and can prevent mistakes like using -1 for setting all bits.
 * Language APIs should thus provide an abstraction that registers bitfields (uint64_t) separately from regular constants (int64_t).
 * @since 4.1
 */
classdb_register_extension_class_integer_constant: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClassIntegerConstant

/**
 * Registers a property on an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * Provided struct can be safely freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.1
 */
classdb_register_extension_class_property: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClassProperty

/**
 * Registers an indexed property on an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * Provided struct can be safely freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.2
 */
classdb_register_extension_class_property_indexed: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClassPropertyIndexed

/**
 * Registers a property group on an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * @since 4.1
 */
classdb_register_extension_class_property_group: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClassPropertyGroup

/**
 * Registers a property subgroup on an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * @since 4.1
 */
classdb_register_extension_class_property_subgroup: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClassPropertySubgroup

/**
 * Registers a signal on an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * Provided structs can be safely freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.1
 */
classdb_register_extension_class_signal: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbRegisterExtensionClassSignal

/**
 * Unregisters an extension class in the ClassDB.
 * Unregistering a parent class before a class that inherits it will result in failure. Inheritors must be unregistered first.
 * @since 4.1
 */
classdb_unregister_extension_class: ExtensionInterfaceClassdbUnregisterExtensionClass

/**
 * Gets the path to the current GDExtension library.
 * @since 4.1
 */
get_library_path: ExtensionInterfaceGetLibraryPath

/**
 * Adds an editor plugin.
 * It's safe to call during initialization.
 * @since 4.1
 */
editor_add_plugin: ExtensionInterfaceEditorAddPlugin

/**
 * Removes an editor plugin.
 * @since 4.1
 */
editor_remove_plugin: ExtensionInterfaceEditorRemovePlugin

/**
 * Loads new XML-formatted documentation data in the editor.
 * The provided pointer can be immediately freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.3
 */
editor_help_load_xml_from_utf8_chars: ExtensionInterfaceEditorHelpLoadXmlFromUtf8Chars

/**
 * Loads new XML-formatted documentation data in the editor.
 * The provided pointer can be immediately freed once the function returns.
 * @since 4.3
 */
editor_help_load_xml_from_utf8_chars_and_len: ExtensionInterfaceEditorHelpLoadXmlFromUtf8CharsAndLen

/**
 * Registers a callback that Godot can call to get the list of all classes (from ClassDB) that may be used by the calling GDExtension.
 * This is used by the editor to generate a build profile (in "Tools" > "Engine Compilation Configuration Editor..." > "Detect from project"),
 * in order to recompile Godot with only the classes used.
 * In the provided callback, the GDExtension should provide the list of classes that _may_ be used statically, thus the time of invocation shouldn't matter.
 * If a GDExtension doesn't register a callback, Godot will assume that it could be using any classes.
 * @since 4.5
 */
editor_register_get_classes_used_callback: ExtensionInterfaceEditorRegisterGetClassesUsedCallback

/**
 * Registers callbacks to be called at different phases of the main loop.
 * @since 4.5
 */
register_main_loop_callbacks: ExtensionInterfaceRegisterMainLoopCallbacks

// The library handle Godot passed to the entry point. Set by init().
library: GDExtensionClassLibraryPtr

// Resolves every interface function pointer from the host Godot instance.
// MUST be called exactly once, from the library entry point, before any other
// binding is used.
